const e={toc:[{id:"why-hair-gets-weak-in-the-first-place",text:"Why Hair Gets Weak in the First Place",level:2},{id:"what-is-an-olaplex-treatment",text:"What Is an Olaplex Treatment?",level:2},{id:"who-benefits-most-from-olaplex",text:"Who Benefits Most from Olaplex?",level:2},{id:"olaplex-with-hair-colour",text:"Olaplex with Hair Colour",level:2},{id:"olaplex-hair-spa-vs-olaplex-add-on",text:"Olaplex Hair Spa vs Olaplex Add-on",level:2},{id:"olaplex-hair-spa",text:"Olaplex Hair Spa",level:3},{id:"olaplex-add-on",text:"Olaplex Add-on",level:3},{id:"how-often-should-you-get-an-olaplex-treatment",text:"How Often Should You Get an Olaplex Treatment?",level:2},{id:"what-olaplex-can-and-cant-do",text:"What Olaplex Can and Can't Do",level:2},{id:"signs-your-hair-could-use-bond-repair",text:"Signs Your Hair Could Use Bond Repair",level:2},{id:"aftercare-that-makes-olaplex-work-harder",text:"Aftercare That Makes Olaplex Work Harder",level:2},{id:"olaplex-for-men",text:"Olaplex for Men",level:2},{id:"book-an-olaplex-treatment-in-bangalore",text:"Book an Olaplex Treatment in Bangalore",level:2}],before:`<p>If you&#39;ve ever coloured, highlighted or bleached your hair, someone has probably recommended Olaplex. It&#39;s one of the most talked-about names in hair care, but many people aren&#39;t sure what it actually does. Put simply, an <strong>Olaplex treatment</strong> helps repair hair that has been weakened from the inside by colour, bleach or heat.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>This guide explains what bond repair means in plain language, who benefits from Olaplex, how it fits with colour services, and the difference between an Olaplex spa and an Olaplex add-on.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="why-hair-gets-weak-in-the-first-place">Why Hair Gets Weak in the First Place</h2>
<p>To understand Olaplex, it helps to know a little about how hair is built.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Each strand of hair is held together by tiny connections called bonds. They give hair its strength and stretch. When bonds are healthy, hair is strong, flexible and shiny.</p>
<p>Some things break these bonds:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bleaching and lightening</strong>, which are needed for highlights, balayage and lighter shades</li>
<li><strong>Colouring</strong>, especially repeated colour over the same lengths</li>
<li><strong>Heat styling</strong>, like daily ironing, curling and hot blow drying</li>
<li><strong>Some chemical treatments</strong> that change the hair&#39;s texture</li>
</ul>
<p>When enough bonds are broken, hair becomes weak. It feels rough and stretchy when wet, snaps easily, tangles more and loses its shine. Regular conditioner can make it feel smoother on the surface, but it doesn&#39;t reach the bonds inside.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="what-is-an-olaplex-treatment">What Is an Olaplex Treatment?</h2>
<p>An Olaplex treatment is bond-building care. Instead of only coating the outside of the hair, it works to help repair and strengthen the hair from within.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>In simple terms:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Conditioners and masks</strong> make hair feel softer on the surface.</li>
<li><strong>Olaplex</strong> focuses on the inner structure, helping restore strength to damaged hair.</li>
</ul>
<p>That&#39;s why Olaplex is often recommended alongside colour and lightening, which are the services most likely to weaken those inner bonds.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="who-benefits-most-from-olaplex">Who Benefits Most from Olaplex?</h2>
<p>An Olaplex treatment is most useful if your hair is:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Coloured</strong>, especially if you colour regularly</li>
<li><strong>Highlighted, balayaged or bleached</strong></li>
<li><strong>Heat-styled often</strong>, such as daily ironing or curling</li>
<li><strong>Breaking easily</strong>, feeling stretchy when wet or rough when dry</li>
<li><strong>Going through a big colour change</strong>, such as going lighter or trying fashion shades</li>
</ul>
<p>If your hair is healthy and simply a little dry, you may not need Olaplex. A nourishing hair spa may be all your hair needs. Your stylist will help you decide at your consultation.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="olaplex-with-hair-colour">Olaplex with Hair Colour</h2>
<p>Colouring and lightening can weaken hair, so the colour appointment is one of the best times to add bond care. At Xing, you can add an Olaplex top-up to any <a href="/services/global-hair-color">hair colour service</a>. It helps protect, repair and strengthen your hair during and after colouring.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Olaplex is especially worth considering if you&#39;re planning:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Balayage or highlights</strong>, which involve lightening (see <a href="/blog/balayage-vs-highlights">balayage vs highlights</a>)</li>
<li><strong>A lighter global colour</strong></li>
<li><strong>Fashion or pastel shades</strong>, which often need pre-lightening</li>
<li><strong>Colour on hair that has already been coloured many times</strong></li>
</ul>
</details>
`,after:`<h2 id="olaplex-hair-spa-vs-olaplex-add-on">Olaplex Hair Spa vs Olaplex Add-on</h2>
<p>At Xing Premium Unisex Salon, you can get Olaplex in two ways as part of a <a href="/services/hair-spa">hair spa</a>.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th>Olaplex Hair Spa</th>
<th>Olaplex Add-on</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><strong>Focus</strong></td>
<td>Bond repair</td>
<td>Bond repair plus another concern</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Best for</strong></td>
<td>Hair mainly damaged by colour, bleach or heat</td>
<td>Treated hair that also needs moisture, frizz control or scalp care</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>How you book it</strong></td>
<td>As its own spa</td>
<td>Added to any hair spa</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="olaplex-hair-spa">Olaplex Hair Spa</h3>
<p>A full spa treatment focused on bond repair. It&#39;s the best choice when damage from colour, bleach or heat is your main concern. Choose it if your hair feels weak, rough and fragile after chemical treatments.</p>
<h3 id="olaplex-add-on">Olaplex Add-on</h3>
<p>Olaplex care added to any other hair spa. Choose this when you have another main concern as well. For example:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Coloured hair that&#39;s also frizzy:</strong> a Moroccan Hair Spa with an Olaplex add-on</li>
<li><strong>Bleached hair with a flaky scalp:</strong> an Anti-Dandruff Hair Spa with an Olaplex add-on</li>
<li><strong>Dry, dull coloured lengths:</strong> a Nourishing Hair Spa with an Olaplex add-on</li>
</ul>
<p>Not sure which spa to pair it with? Our guide to the <a href="/blog/types-of-hair-spa">types of hair spa</a> explains each one.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="how-often-should-you-get-an-olaplex-treatment">How Often Should You Get an Olaplex Treatment?</h2>
<p>This depends on how damaged your hair is and how often you colour or heat-style it. A few general guidelines:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>With every colour or lightening service:</strong> an Olaplex top-up helps protect your hair at the point it&#39;s most at risk.</li>
<li><strong>When repairing damaged hair:</strong> a short course of spas works better than a single one. For hair spas, we recommend at least three sittings, two to three weeks apart, then monthly maintenance.</li>
<li><strong>For maintenance:</strong> add Olaplex to your regular spa if your hair is coloured or bleached.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your stylist will suggest a plan that suits your hair.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="what-olaplex-can-and-cant-do">What Olaplex Can and Can&#39;t Do</h2>
<p>It&#39;s worth having realistic expectations.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p><strong>Olaplex can help:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Make damaged hair feel stronger and less fragile</li>
<li>Reduce breakage from colour, bleach and heat</li>
<li>Improve how hair feels and behaves after chemical services</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Olaplex can&#39;t:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Undo all damage in one session if hair is badly broken</li>
<li>Replace trims, as split ends still need cutting</li>
<li>Make up for harsh daily habits, like very hot tools without heat protection</li>
</ul>
<p>The best results come from Olaplex combined with good aftercare.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="signs-your-hair-could-use-bond-repair">Signs Your Hair Could Use Bond Repair</h2>
<p>Not sure if your hair is damaged enough to need Olaplex? These are common signs:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>It stretches when wet</strong> and doesn&#39;t spring back</li>
<li><strong>It feels rough or gummy</strong> after lightening</li>
<li><strong>It snaps easily</strong> when brushed or styled</li>
<li><strong>It tangles more than it used to</strong></li>
<li><strong>It looks dull</strong> even after conditioning</li>
<li><strong>The ends feel straw-like</strong> and split quickly</li>
</ul>
<p>If several of these sound familiar, and especially if your hair is coloured or bleached, an Olaplex Hair Spa or an Olaplex add-on is worth discussing with your stylist. They can check your hair and tell you how much repair it needs.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="aftercare-that-makes-olaplex-work-harder">Aftercare That Makes Olaplex Work Harder</h2>
<p>To get the most from your Olaplex treatment:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li>Use a colour-safe, sulphate-free shampoo</li>
<li>Always use a heat protectant before blow drying, ironing or curling</li>
<li>Lower the heat on your tools where you can</li>
<li>Rinse with cool or lukewarm water</li>
<li>Book regular hair spas to keep lengths nourished</li>
<li>Get regular trims to remove split ends</li>
</ul>
<p>Our guide on <a href="/blog/make-hair-colour-last">how to make hair colour last</a> has more tips for coloured hair.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="olaplex-for-men">Olaplex for Men</h2>
<p>Men colour and heat-style their hair too, whether it&#39;s grey coverage, highlights or a fashion shade. An Olaplex treatment works the same way on men&#39;s hair, and our hair spas and colour services are available for men and women. If your hair feels rough or brittle after colouring, ask about adding Olaplex.</p>
<h2 id="book-an-olaplex-treatment-in-bangalore">Book an Olaplex Treatment in Bangalore</h2>
<p>If your hair has been through colour, bleach or a lot of heat styling, an Olaplex treatment is one of the most effective ways to help it feel strong and healthy again. Book it as a full spa, add it to any spa, or add it to your next colour appointment.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Visit us at Xing Premium Unisex Salon in Sarjapur Road, HSR Layout or Brookfield, and tell us about your hair on WhatsApp so we can recommend the right Olaplex option.</p>
</details>
`,takeaways:["Olaplex is a bond-building treatment that helps repair and strengthen hair weakened by colour, bleach or heat.","It's most useful for coloured, highlighted, bleached or heavily heat-styled hair.","Adding Olaplex to a colour service helps protect hair during and after colouring.","Choose a full Olaplex Hair Spa for repair, or add Olaplex to any spa or colour service.","Olaplex works best alongside good aftercare: gentle shampoo, heat protection and regular spas."],faqs:[{q:"What does an Olaplex treatment do?",a:"Olaplex is a bond-building treatment. It helps repair and strengthen hair that has been weakened by colouring, bleaching or heat styling, so hair feels healthier and breaks less."},{q:"Do I need Olaplex if I don't colour my hair?",a:"Not always. Olaplex is most useful for chemically treated or heavily heat-styled hair. If your hair is simply dry, a nourishing hair spa may be all you need. Your stylist can advise you."},{q:"Can I add Olaplex to my hair colour appointment?",a:"Yes. At Xing, you can add an Olaplex top-up to any hair colour service."},{q:"What is the difference between an Olaplex spa and an Olaplex add-on?",a:"An Olaplex Hair Spa is a full spa treatment focused on bond repair. An Olaplex add-on adds Olaplex care to any other hair spa, so you can treat another concern like frizz at the same time."}]};export{e as default};
